␀␀␀␀␀␀0␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>fps60</title>
<link rel="icon" href="/icon.png">
<link rel="stylesheet" href="/ui/common.css">
<style>
  .game-head { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; gap: 8px;
               align-items: baseline; }
  .game-name { font-weight: 600; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .patch { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between;
           gap: 12px; padding-top: 10px; margin-top: 10px;
           border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .patch-info { min-width: 0; }
  .patch-name { font-weight: 500; }
  .log-row { font-size: 13px; padding: 6px 0; border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .log-row:first-child { border-top: 0; }
  @media (min-width: 1100px) {
    #games { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(2, minmax(0, 1fr));
             gap: 14px; align-items: start; }
    #games .card { margin-bottom: 0; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<main>
  <header>
    <div class="brand"><img src="/icon.png" alt=""><h1>fps60</h1></div>
    <span class="sub" id="summary">Loadingâ€¦</span>
  </header>
  <nav class="tabs" id="tabs"></nav>
  <div id="error"></div>

  <section id="tab-games" role="tabpanel">
    <div class="bar">
      <input type="search" id="search" placeholder="Search games or title IDs"
             aria-label="Search games">
      <select id="filter" aria-label="Filter">
        <option value="patched">Games with a 60 FPS patch</option>
        <option value="tested">Tested on PS5</option>
        <option value="all">All installed games</option>
      </select>
      <button id="rescan" type="button">Rescan</button>
    </div>

    <div id="games"></div>

    <h2>Activity</h2>
    <div class="card" id="log"></div>

    <p class="hint">
      Patches apply when the game starts. Turning one on while the game runs
      applies it right away, but some games only read their frame-rate setting
      at boot, so restart the game if nothing changes. Turning a patch off takes
      effect the next time the game starts. Use patches in offline play only.
      The Logs tab shows every step in detail.
    </p>
  </section>
</main>

<script src="/ui/common.js"></script>
<script>
"use strict";
const { $, el, chip, call, showError } = App;
let state = null;
let busy = false;

// Patches confirmed working on a real PS5 (see "Tested games" in the README).
// Each entry covers every regional title ID of the game.
const TESTED = [
  { game: "Gravity Rush 2", patch: "60 FPS", version: "01.11",
    tids: ["CUSA00547", "CUSA03694", "CUSA04934", "CUSA04943"] },
  { game: "The Order: 1886", patch: "60 FPS Unlock", version: "01.02",
    tids: ["CUSA00035", "CUSA00070", "CUSA00076", "CUSA00100", "CUSA00670", "CUSA00785"] },
];
const testedFor = (tid, name) =>
  TESTED.find((t) => t.patch === name && t.tids.includes(tid));
const gameTested = (g) => g.patches.some((p) => testedFor(g.tid, p.name));

async function refresh() {
  if (busy) return;
  try {
    const fresh = await call("GET", "/api/state");
    // A toggle started while this was in flight; its own reply is newer.
    if (busy) return;
    state = fresh;
    showError("");
    render();
  } catch (e) {
    showError("Can't reach fps60 on the console: " + e.message);
  }
}

async function rescan() {
  state = await call("POST", "/api/rescan");
  showError("");
  render();
}

async function toggle(game, patch, on, input) {
  busy = true;
  input.disabled = true;
  try {
    const q = new URLSearchParams({ tid: game.tid, name: patch.name, on: on ? "1" : "0" });
    state = await call("POST", "/api/toggle?" + q);
    showError("");
  } catch (e) {
    showError("Couldn't change " + patch.name + ": " + e.message);
  }
  busy = false;
  render();
}

function patchRow(game, patch) {
  const row = el("div", "patch");
  const info = el("div", "patch-info");
  const name = el("div", "patch-name", patch.name);
  const supported = [...new Set(patch.versions.filter((v) => v.supported).map((v) => v.appver))];
  const running = state.running.some((r) => r.tid === game.tid);

  if (patch.available) {
    name.append(chip("ok", "Matches your version"));
  } else if (supported.length) {
    name.append(chip("warn", "Needs version " + supported.join(", ")));
  } else {
    name.append(chip("bad", "Not supported by fps60"));
  }
  const tested = testedFor(game.tid, patch.name);
  if (tested) {
    const c = chip("info", "Tested on PS5");
    c.title = "Confirmed working on a PS5 with game version " + tested.version;
    name.append(c);
  }
  if (patch.enabled && running) name.append(chip("ok", "Game running"));
  info.append(name);

  const by = patch.author ? "by " + patch.author : "";
  const note = [by, patch.note].filter(Boolean).join(" Â· ");
  if (note) info.append(el("div", "note", note));

  const label = el("label", "switch");
  const input = el("input");
  input.type = "checkbox";
  input.checked = patch.enabled;
  input.disabled = !patch.available && !patch.enabled;
  input.setAttribute("aria-label", patch.name + " for " + (game.name || game.tid));
  input.addEventListener("change", () => toggle(game, patch, input.checked, input));
  label.append(input, el("span", "slider"));

  row.append(info, label);
  return row;
}

function render() {
  if (!state) return;
  App.renderSettings();
  const q = $("search").value.trim().toLowerCase();
  const filter = $("filter").value;
  const games = state.games
    .filter((g) => filter === "all" || (filter === "tested" ? gameTested(g) : g.patches.length))
    .filter((g) => !q || (g.name + " " + g.tid).toLowerCase().includes(q))
    .sort((a, b) =>
      (b.patches.some((p) => p.available) - a.patches.some((p) => p.available)) ||
      (gameTested(b) - gameTested(a)) ||
      (a.name || a.tid).localeCompare(b.name || b.tid));

  const withPatch = state.games.filter((g) => g.patches.some((p) => p.available)).length;
  $("summary").textContent = state.games.length + " games installed Â· " +
    withPatch + " with a 60 FPS patch for your version";

  const list = $("games");
  list.replaceChildren();
  if (!games.length) {
    list.append(el("div", "card empty", state.games.length
      ? "No matching games."
      : "No installed games found. Try Rescan."));
  }
  for (const g of games) {
    const card = el("div", "card");
    const head = el("div", "game-head");
    head.append(el("div", "game-name", g.name || g.tid),
      el("div", "meta", [g.tid, g.ps5 ? "PS5" : "PS4", g.version && "v" + g.version]
        .filter(Boolean).join(" Â· ")));
    card.append(head);
    if (!g.patches.length) card.append(el("div", "note", "No known frame-rate patch."));
    for (const p of g.patches) card.append(patchRow(g, p));
    list.append(card);
  }

  const log = $("log");
  log.replaceChildren();
  if (!state.log.length) log.append(el("div", "empty", "Nothing applied yet."));
  for (const e of state.log) {
    const row = el("div", "log-row");
    row.append(chip(e.ok ? "ok" : "bad", e.ok ? "Applied" : "Failed"));
    row.append(" " + (e.title || e.tid) + " Â· " + e.name + " (v" + e.version + "): " + e.msg);
    log.append(row);
  }
}

$("search").addEventListener("input", render);
$("filter").addEventListener("change", render);
$("rescan").addEventListener("click", () => rescan().catch(
  (e) => showError("Rescan failed: " + e.message)));

App.init({
  name: "fps60",
  tabs: [{ id: "games", label: "Games" }],
  logTools: [{
    label: "Diagnose",
    title: "Log every process and the modules of game processes",
    onClick: () => call("POST", "/api/diagnose"),
  }],
  settings: [{
    title: "Rescan installed games",
    note: "Run this after installing or updating a game.",
    button: "Rescan",
    onClick: rescan,
  }],
  stopNote: "Patches already applied stay in running games.",
  about: () => state ? [
    ["Patches", state.dbPatches + " frame-rate patches"],
    ["Settings file", "/data/fps60/enabled.txt"],
  ] : [],
});

refresh();
setInterval(refresh, 3000);
</script>
</body>
</html>
